  "evidencia": "Page: Sylvia Plath. Sentence: Sylvia Plath ( ; October 27, 1932 – February 11, 1963) was an American poet, novelist, and short story writer.\nPage: Sylvia Plath. Sentence: Born in Boston, she studied at Smith College and Newnham College at the University of Cambridge before receiving acclaim as a poet and writer.\nPage: Sylvia Plath. Sentence: She married fellow poet Ted Hughes in 1956, and they lived together in the United States and then in England.\nPage: Sylvia Plath. Sentence: They had two children, Frieda and Nicholas, before separating in 1962.\nPage: Sylvia Plath. Sentence: Plath was clinically depressed for most of her adult life, and was treated multiple times with electroconvulsive therapy (ECT).\nPage: Sylvia Plath. Sentence: She committed suicide in 1963.\nPage: Michael Cunningham. Sentence: Michael Cunningham (born November 6, 1952) is a U.S. novelist and screenwriter.\nPage: Michael Cunningham. Sentence: He is best known for his 1998 novel \"The Hours\", which won the Pulitzer Prize for Fiction and the PEN/Faulkner Award in 1999.\nPage: The Bell Jar. Sentence: The Bell Jar is the only novel written by the American writer and poet Sylvia Plath.",
